FILES
-----

build-aux/linux/appimage/
├── appimage.readme           This file
├── config.sh                 Settings: Qt version, QET branch, options
├── common.sh                 Shared functions
├── 01-build-host.sh          Host packages, Qt 6, AppImage tools
├── 02-build-qet.sh           KDE Frameworks (once), then QElectroTech
├── 03-build-appimage.sh      Bundle and AppImage file
├── makeall.sh                01 + 02 + 03 : everything from scratch
├── update.sh                 02 + 03 : rebuild QET and the AppImage
└── data
    ├── AppRun                Launcher inside the AppImage
    └── qt.conf               Qt plugins/translations paths in the bundle


REQUIREMENTS
------------

- Ubuntu or Xubuntu 24.04 x86_64. A virtual machine is fine (4 cores,
  8 GB RAM and 30 GB of disk recommended).
- A normal user with sudo rights. Do NOT run the scripts as root: only the
  apt commands in 01-build-host.sh use sudo. Everything else is built and
  assembled in $HOME/qet-appimage-work.
- Internet access to: Ubuntu mirrors, PyPI (aqtinstall), the Qt download
  mirrors, invent.kde.org (KDE Frameworks) and github.com (QET sources,
  appimagetool, excludelist).
- In a VM, disable the screen locker and the suspend before a long build
  (Xfce: Settings > Screensaver and Settings > Power Manager), or:
    sudo systemctl mask sleep.target suspend.target hibernate.target hybrid-sleep.target


CONFIGURATION (config.sh)
-------------------------

QT_FROM          aqt    : official Qt binaries installed with aqtinstall
                          (default, recommended)
                 system : Ubuntu's Qt 6.4.2. QET master does not compile
                          with it any more: only for older branches.
QT_VERSION       Qt version installed by aqt (default 6.11.2).
QT_AQT_MODULES   Extra Qt modules: qtpdf (PDF page import), qtimageformats.
QET_VERSION      QET branch or tag to package (default master).
QET_WITH_KF      1 : build with KCoreAddons/KWidgetsAddons (default).
                 0 : use QET's own replacements (sources/ui/nokde).
KF_VERSION       KDE Frameworks tag (default v6.10.0, as in
                 cmake/fetch_kdeaddons.cmake).
QET_SPACEMOUSE   1 : 3D mouse support through hidapi.
QET_DEBUG        1 : keep the debug symbols of the qelectrotech binary.
QET_SIGN         1 : detached GPG signature (.sig) of the AppImage.
QET_UPLOAD       1 : rsync the AppImage to QET_UPLOADURL:QET_UPLOADDIR.


USAGE
-----

First build, from this directory:

    ./makeall.sh

Next builds (host, Qt and KDE Frameworks already in place):

    ./update.sh

The AppImage and its SHA256 file are written in ./bundle/ :

    QElectroTech_<major.minor.micro>-r<revision>-x86_64.AppImage
    QElectroTech_<major.minor.micro>-r<revision>-x86_64.AppImage-SHA256.txt

The revision number is computed as in the former packaging script:
git rev-list HEAD --count + 473.

The logs of each step are in ./logs/.


HOW IT WORKS
------------

* 01-build-host.sh
  - installs the build packages with apt (compiler, CMake, Ninja, patchelf,
    SQLite, xcb/wayland/xkbcommon, CUPS, OpenSSL...);
  - installs Qt with aqtinstall in $HOME/qet-appimage-work/Qt;
  - downloads appimagetool (static runtime) and the AppImage excludelist.

* 02-build-qet.sh
  - builds ECM, KCoreAddons and KWidgetsAddons once, statically, against the
    same Qt, in $HOME/qet-appimage-work/kf6 (QET's own BUILD_KF=ON fetch does
    not work: kcoreaddons cannot find the fetched ECM);
  - clones or updates QET in $HOME/qet-appimage-work/build, builds it with
    -DBUILD_WITH_KF=ON -DBUILD_KF=OFF -DPACKAGE_TESTS=OFF;
  - installs it with DESTDIR in the AppDir, prefix /usr.

* 03-build-appimage.sh
  - copies the Qt plugins QET needs: platforms (xcb, wayland), platform
    themes, input methods, xcb GL, wayland integrations, image formats,
    SVG icon engine, print support (CUPS), TLS, and the SQLite driver only;
  - copies the Qt translations (qt_*.qm, qtbase_*.qm);
  - collects the shared libraries with ldd, minus the libraries of the
    excludelist (glibc, libstdc++, libGL/libEGL, X11, fontconfig...):
    bundling libGL/libEGL would break the host graphics drivers;
  - sets the RPATHs with patchelf ($ORIGIN): LD_LIBRARY_PATH is not used,
    so the programs QET starts (browser, PDF viewer, xdg-open) keep the
    host libraries;
  - strips the binaries and runs appimagetool.

* data/AppRun
  QET is built with absolute /usr/share/qelectrotech paths. AppRun gives it
  the paths inside the AppImage with --common-elements-dir,
  --common-tbt-dir and --lang-dir.


CONTINUOUS INTEGRATION
----------------------

.github/workflows/linux-appimage.yml runs these scripts on an ubuntu-24.04
GitHub runner. It is called by windows-msi.yml, so it only runs when the
Windows CI/CD runs, in parallel with the MSI build:

    Windows Build -> windows-msi.yml -> build-msi       \
                                     -> build-appimage   -> deploy-pages

- QET_SOURCE_DIR points the scripts to the workflow's checkout, built as
  it is, and CI=true skips the dist-upgrade.
- Qt ($QT_ROOT) and the KDE Frameworks ($KF_PREFIX) are kept in the
  GitHub Actions cache, keyed by QT_VERSION and KF_VERSION: only QET is
  rebuilt on each run.
- The AppImage and its SHA256 file replace the previous ones on the
  nightly-qt6 release, and deploy-pages adds a Linux section to
  https://qelectrotech.github.io/qelectrotech-source-mirror/
- An AppImage failure never blocks the Windows part of the page.


COMPATIBILITY
-------------

An AppImage only runs on systems whose glibc is at least as recent as the
build host's. Built on Ubuntu 24.04 (glibc 2.39), it runs on Ubuntu 24.04
and later, Debian 13 and later, Fedora 40 and later, current Arch Linux and
openSUSE Tumbleweed. It does NOT run on Ubuntu 22.04 or Debian 12.

No libfuse2 is needed on the target: appimagetool uses the static type2
runtime.


AT RUN-TIME ON TARGET COMPUTER
------------------------------

    chmod +x QElectroTech_*.AppImage
    ./QElectroTech_*.AppImage              run QElectroTech
    ./QElectroTech_*.AppImage file.qet     open a project
    ./QElectroTech_*.AppImage debug        run QElectroTech in gdb
    ./QElectroTech_*.AppImage help         show these options

To integrate the AppImage into the desktop menu and file associations, use
Gear Lever or AppImageLauncher.


TROUBLESHOOTING
---------------

- "This application failed to start because no Qt platform plugin could be
  initialized": run with QT_DEBUG_PLUGINS=1 to see which library is missing,
  then add it to the bundle or check that it is not wrongly excluded.
- Unresolved libraries: 03-build-appimage.sh prints
  "WARNING: unresolved dependencies" with the missing names.
- Wayland: force X11 with QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb if a compositor misbehaves.


